    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7a5de9d1_04266ece",
        "filename": "keystone/assignment/routers.py",
        "patchSetId": 61
      },
      "lineNbr": 79,
      "author": {
        "id": 10608
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-01-27T22:24:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The \"prior_\" here (and throughout) is not good REST in my opinion. At least not optimal. These are \"roles\", and should use that existing noun.\n\nAnd you should have a way to trace these relationships in both directions, not just one.\n\nI would suggest:\n\nGET /role?implied_by\u003d{role_id}\nGET /role?implies\u003d{role_id}",
      "revId": "d52d9524d84a04230235887ec316afb8fdd3c1dd",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7a5de9d1_11122f63",
        "filename": "keystone/assignment/routers.py",
        "patchSetId": 61
      },
      "lineNbr": 79,
      "author": {
        "id": 1916
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-01-27T22:53:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "too late to change the spec would it?",
      "parentUuid": "7a5de9d1_04266ece",
      "revId": "d52d9524d84a04230235887ec316afb8fdd3c1dd",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7a5de9d1_7fa1efa8",
        "filename": "keystone/assignment/routers.py",
        "patchSetId": 61
      },
      "lineNbr": 91,
      "author": {
        "id": 10608
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-01-27T22:24:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "continuing the comment above, these would be:\n\nPATCH /role/{role_id} adding or removing things from new \"implied_by\" and \"implies\" elements in the json for a role to create and delete these relationships. Or POST /role_inferences and DELETE /role_inferences/{role_inference_id}.\n\nYou may not have a replacement for check_implied_role... Instead, call GET /role?implies\u003d{role_id} and parse the response to see whether what you\u0027re looking for is there. Or you could GET /role_inferences?prior_role\u003d{role_id}\u0026implied_role\u003d{role_id} and expect 404 if that doesn\u0027t exist.\n\nGET /role/{role_id} would replace get_implied_role",
      "revId": "d52d9524d84a04230235887ec316afb8fdd3c1dd",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
